src/withdraws/Ethena.sol:_finalizeCooldown:39|class=C15|High|While Ethena's sUSDe.cooldownDuration() is 0, any unprivileged actor calls the permissionless AbstractLendingRouter.forceWithdraw on an unhealthy PendlePT_sUSDe position (which enters PendlePT._initiateWithdraw and hands sUSDe to EthenaWithdrawRequestManager, whose holder instantly redeems it to USDe), then triggers finalization: _finalizeCooldown snapshots balanceBefore after the USDe has already landed and skips unstake because cooldownEnd==0, so tokensClaimed = 0 with finalized = true, which _finalizeWithdraw latches permanently via s.totalWithdraw = 0 / require(s.finalized == false), causing _redeemShares to burn the victim's shares for zero assets and strand the USDe on the clone.|src/withdraws/Ethena.sol
